BTEC IT Units – Learning Portfolio
This repository documents the IT topics I have studied as part of my BTEC IT course. Each section explains what the unit covers and the skills or knowledge I have developed.

Unit 01 – The Online World
This unit covers how people use the internet and online services. 
It includes understanding websites, online communication, digital services, and how information moves around the online world. 
It also introduces safe and responsible use of the internet, including awareness of online risks.

Unit 02 – Technology Systems
This unit looks at the main parts of computer systems and how they work together. 
It covers hardware, software, input and output devices, storage, and the role of different components. 
It helps build an understanding of how a computer system processes information and how its parts support users.

Unit 03 – A Digital Portfolio
This unit focuses on creating a digital portfolio to present work and information. 
It involves organising content clearly, choosing suitable layouts, and using digital tools to show skills and completed projects. 
My website-development practice also includes using HTML and CSS, building navigation between pages, and testing pages in Visual Studio Code with Live Server.

Unit 09 – Spreadsheet Development
This unit covers creating and using spreadsheets to organise, calculate, and present data. 
It includes working with rows and columns, using formulas and functions, formatting cells, and presenting information so it is easy to understand. 
Spreadsheets can be used to solve problems, track information, and support decisions.

Unit 10 – Database Development
This unit introduces databases and how they are used to store and manage information. 
It covers organising data into tables, using fields and records, creating relationships between data, and retrieving information with queries. 
A well-designed database helps keep information organised, accurate, and easier to search.

Unit 11 – Computer Networks
This unit covers how computers and other devices connect and communicate. 
It includes network types, network devices, communication methods, protocols, and the reasons organisations use networks to share data and resources.
It also introduces network reliability and security, including the importance of protecting information as it travels between devices.

Unit 16 – Automated Computer Systems
This unit looks at systems that carry out tasks automatically with limited direct human input. 
It includes understanding inputs, processes, and outputs, as well as the use of sensors and control systems. 
Automated systems are used in areas such as manufacturing, monitoring, and everyday technology.

Unit 22 – Computer Security in Practice
This unit focuses on practical computer security and ways to protect systems and information. 
It includes identifying threats and vulnerabilities, understanding risks, and considering protective measures such as access controls, strong authentication, firewalls, updates, and data protection. 
It also highlights the importance of choosing security measures that suit the system and its users.

Skills and tools connected to my IT studies
- Web development: HTML, CSS, basic JavaScript concepts, page structure, styling, and navigation.
- Digital portfolio development: organising and presenting coursework and projects.
- Data handling: spreadsheets, formulas, tables, and database concepts.
- Computer systems: understanding hardware, software, input/output, and storage.
- Networking: network concepts, devices, protocols, and basic security awareness.
- Cybersecurity: recognising threats, vulnerabilities, and ways to reduce risk.
- Tools: Visual Studio Code and Live Server for building and testing web pages.

